{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01E8ysqL35dAriFmPsmmTRWt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `congestion_control_algorithms()` returns an empty slice if `register_all_congestion_control_algorithms()` hasn't been called. The test `cubic()` calls `get_congestion_algorithm(\"cubic\")` which would return `None` if the registry is empty. This is a pre-existing issue not caused by my changes.\n\nLet me verify by checking the git blame or looking at when these tests were introduced vs when the cubic algorithm was registered. Actually, the simplest verification is to check if these tests already fail on the main branch or on the most recent commit (before my changes).\n\nSince I can't git stash without approval, let me just check a specific test that uses `register_all_congestion_control_algorithms`:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1771,"cache_read_input_tokens":136492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1771},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0935a79a-3385-490e-8044-a2b7bb8dca0a","uuid":"61599fa7-4d31-4af7-aee3-0933c479e7c6"}
