{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01LArfaQ3duXWPj5yx9haZMC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that the congestion test calls `get_congestion_algorithm(\"cubic\")` but doesn't first call `register_all_congestion_control_algorithms()`. This is a pre-existing issue in the test framework, not something I introduced.\n\nThese tests rely on a global state `CC_ALGORITHM_REGISTRY` being initialized. When tests run in parallel (which is the default for Rust tests), the order matters. If some test that calls `register_all_congestion_control_algorithms()` runs first, it initializes the registry and other tests can use it. If the congestion test runs before that, it fails.\n\n\nMy changes are completely unrelated to this—I only added methods to `CubicState`, a doc comment to `Dualq::scheduler`, and some ECH helper functions, none of which would affect algorithm registration. Let me trace through the test to confirm the cubic algorithm itself isn't being affected by my modifications.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1582,"cache_read_input_tokens":138263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1582},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0935a79a-3385-490e-8044-a2b7bb8dca0a","uuid":"3e2aac4e-8690-4867-85f2-e55afedf2e13"}
